### IV. JAVASCRIPT & STYLESHEET SCOPE MAPPING

1. JAVASCRIPT ASSET MANAGEMENT (`assets/js/`):
   - All client-side JavaScript must reside in external `.js` files within `assets/js/`. Embedded `<script>` blocks inside PHP templates are strictly prohibited for new code. (Legacy inline blocks remain only until refactored; any that survive MUST include the opt-out attributes via `<script <?php echo SYWAT_SCRIPT_OPTOUT_ATTRS; ?>>`.)
   - Enqueue rules:
     - Script handles MUST start with `sywat-` (this automatically applies the WP Rocket / Cloudflare / LiteSpeed opt-out attributes).
     - URLs MUST be built from `SYWAT_PLUGIN_URL . 'assets/js/...'`. NEVER `site_url()`, `plugins_url( '../../...' )` or relative paths (root cause of the 6.7.0 score-entry 404).
     - Version MUST be `SYWAT_PLUGIN_VERSION` (or `filemtime()`), never a hand-typed number.
     - Enqueue only where needed: inside the shortcode render function, or on `wp_enqueue_scripts` guarded by `sywat_should_load_module_assets()`. NEVER on `admin_enqueue_scripts` unless the module has its own wp-admin screen, and then only on that screen's hook.
     - Load in the footer (`true`), with no jQuery dependency. Write vanilla JS only; jQuery is not loaded by the plugin.
     - Pass server data with `wp_localize_script()` or `wp_add_inline_script( ..., 'before' )`. AJAX URLs come from `window.ajaxurl` (set by the modal manager) or localized data, never a hard-coded `'/wp-admin/admin-ajax.php'`.
   - Global namespace:
     - New functions MUST NOT be added as bare globals. Expose them under `window.SYWAT.<module>` or use delegated listeners.
     - Any unavoidable global MUST carry a module-unique `sywat<Module>` prefix (e.g., `sywatRosterHandleDivisionChange`). Generic names (`openModal`, `handleStyleRestrictions`) are prohibited because they collide across modules.
   - Event binding:
     - NEW markup MUST NOT use inline `onclick`/`onchange`/`oninput`/`onsubmit` attributes. Use `data-sywat-action="..."` attributes with one delegated listener per module file (`document.addEventListener('click', ...)`), so markup never calls code that an optimizer has not loaded yet.
     - Global keyboard handlers are reserved for the modal manager (Escape, Tab trap). Modules must not add document-level `keydown` listeners.
   - JS must NEVER manipulate inline styles via `element.style.*`, `element.style.cssText` or `element.setAttribute('style', ...)`. Visibility is driven strictly by toggling CSS classes (`.classList.add('sywat-hidden')`, `.remove()`). Exception: dynamic progress bar widths (`fill.style.width = X%`).

2. STYLESHEET SCOPE MAP (`assets/css/`):
   - All visual styling must reside in external stylesheets: `sywat-buttons.css`, `sywat-core.css`, `sywat-modals.css`, `sywat-public.css`, `sywat-tables.css`, `sywat-toolbar.css`.
   - Design tokens (CSS custom properties) live ONLY in the `:root` block at the top of `sywat-core.css`. Modal stacking variables live ONLY in `sywat-modals.css`.
   - Stylesheets are enqueued centrally by `class-sywat-frontend.php`. Modules must not enqueue their own CSS files or add `wp_add_inline_style()` blocks.

